WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.570
In the Tanakh, Samuel takes a horn of
oil and anoints the young David as king.

2
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:11.030
That is the root of the word Messiah:
the Hebrew mashiach means anointed.

3
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.500
And in the book of Malachi, Elijah is
the herald who comes before the great and

4
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.060
terrible day.

5
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.790
So how would Jews know
the Messiah had come?

6
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.000
And what would the world look like?

7
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.350
In this mission, you'll read
the prophets Isaiah and Micah,

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.500
and meet the test Maimonides
set for the Messiah.

9
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.320
Then you'll compare how Orthodox and
Reform Jews hope for the future today.

10
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.120
Your mission: find out how Jews
would recognise the Messiah,

11
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.840
and what the world would look like.
